<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!--
    ToolCommandList — the house "CHAT COMMANDS" block: one read-only section that
    says which chat verbs the tool on this page actually answers to.

    ★ WHY IT EXISTS. Every pre-build tool has chat verbs and most of them were
    invisible: the four shapes Counters synthesizes by concatenation
    (!deaths+ / !deaths- / !setdeaths / !resetdeaths), the viewer queue's four
    moderator sub-verbs, Loyalty's raffle draw / cancel and duel accept / decline,
    Automod's !permit — none of those appear in any field on any panel, because no
    field holds them. The streamer's only way to learn them was the source. This
    control renders BuiltInCommandCatalog's answer, which derives every one of them
    from the tool's own config. Whether a given parser matches that config field or
    a hard-coded literal is the catalogue's invariant to keep, not this control's —
    see the contract note at the top of BuiltInCommandCatalog.cs, which names the
    call sites it binds.

    ═══════════════ THE GEOMETRY, AND WHY IT IS WHAT IT IS ═══════════════

    Section header verbatim from UserManagementView.xaml:565-576 — eyebrow in
    ToolEyebrowTextStyle, then a 1px CoalDividerBrush hairline filling the rest of
    the row. Rows then sit in one ToolSectionCardStyle border, which is the house
    grammar (a section is a header followed by cards, never a header followed by
    loose rows).

    THREE COLUMNS, TWO OF THEM FIXED, and that is deliberate. An ItemsRepeater
    measures every row independently, so `Auto` columns do NOT align down the list —
    each row would size its own verb column and the whole block would read as ragged
    text instead of a table. The verb and role columns are therefore pixel-fixed
    (the ToolActivityFeed 86/38/* precedent) and both WRAP rather than trim: a verb
    the streamer has to type must never be shown with an ellipsis, and the widest
    honest role summary — "Sub · VIP · Mod · Broadcaster · Regular" — does not fit
    one line at any column width this page can spare.

    NO ScrollViewer AND NO HEIGHT. The control is designed to sit inside a page's
    existing detail scroller; a nested scroll region there is the classic trapped-
    wheel bug, and a MaxHeight would hide rows on exactly the tools that have the
    most verbs. It grows to its content and lets the page scroll. Virtualization is
    given up along with the height cap, which is free at this scale — the largest
    catalogue (Loyalty) is nineteen rows.

    THE DIMMED TREATMENT IS TWO SIGNALS, not one. A disabled row drops to 45%
    opacity AND gains an "OFF" tag under the verb. Opacity alone is a
    contrast-only cue, which is the weakest kind and the first one lost on a
    washed-out stream monitor; the tag says it in a word.
-->
<UserControl
    x:Class="Phoenix.Controls.Hub.WinUI.Panels.Common.ToolCommandList"
    xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
    xmlns:local="using:Phoenix.Controls.Hub.WinUI.Panels.Common"
    xmlns:loc="using:Phoenix.Controls.Hub.WinUI.Localization">

    <UserControl.Resources>
        <ResourceDictionary>
            <ResourceDictionary.MergedDictionaries>
                <!-- Keyed-only shell styles, merged HERE rather than relied upon from
                     the host page: this control is dropped into twelve pages and must
                     not depend on which dictionaries each of them happens to merge.
                     Never merged into App.xaml — see the ToolShellStyles header. -->
                <ResourceDictionary Source="ms-appx:///Panels/Common/ToolShellStyles.xaml" />
            </ResourceDictionary.MergedDictionaries>
        </ResourceDictionary>
    </UserControl.Resources>

    <StackPanel Spacing="8">

        <!-- Section header: eyebrow + hairline. -->
        <Grid ColumnSpacing="10">
            <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto" />
                <ColumnDefinition Width="*" />
            </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
            <TextBlock x:Name="TitleText"
                       Grid.Column="0"
                       Text="CHAT COMMANDS"
                       Style="{StaticResource ToolEyebrowTextStyle}"
                       VerticalAlignment="Center" />
            <Border Grid.Column="1" Height="1"
                    Background="{StaticResource CoalDividerBrush}"
                    VerticalAlignment="Center" />
        </Grid>

        <Border Style="{StaticResource ToolSectionCardStyle}">
            <Grid>
                <!-- Empty state. A command list is not an activity feed: "this tool
                     answers no chat verbs" is a real, reachable configuration (a
                     Counters tool with no counters, a soundboard with no rows) and
                     the catalogue also drops any verb whose word is blank, because a
                     blank word provably matches nothing. A bare header with no rows
                     under it reads as a broken panel; this sentence reads as the
                     answer it is. -->
                <TextBlock x:Name="EmptyText"
                           Text="No chat commands are configured."
                           Style="{StaticResource ToolMonoHintTextStyle}"
                           Visibility="Collapsed"
                           loc:Localize.Key="panel.common.commands.empty.body" />

                <ItemsRepeater x:Name="Rows"
                               local:RowDataContext.Supply="True">
                    <ItemsRepeater.ItemTemplate>
                        <DataTemplate x:DataType="local:ToolCommandRowVm">
                            <!-- Tag="{x:Bind}" per the house rule for new row
                                 templates. Nothing in this control handles a row
                                 today (it is read-only), so this is the cheap half of
                                 the pair that makes adding one — copy the verb,
                                 jump to the field — a one-line change instead of a
                                 silent null-DataContext hunt. -->
                            <Grid Tag="{x:Bind}"
                                  Opacity="{x:Bind RowOpacity}"
                                  Padding="0,5"
                                  ColumnSpacing="12"
                                  BorderBrush="{StaticResource CoalDividerBrush}"
                                  BorderThickness="0,0,0,1">
                                <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                                    <ColumnDefinition Width="150" />
                                    <ColumnDefinition Width="*" />
                                    <ColumnDefinition Width="130" />
                                </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>

                                <StackPanel Grid.Column="0" Spacing="2">
                                    <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind DisplayVerb}"
                                               FontFamily="{StaticResource MonoFont}"
                                               FontSize="11"
                                               TextWrapping="Wrap"
                                               Foreground="{StaticResource EmberPrimaryBrush}" />
                                    <TextBlock Text="OFF"
                                               Visibility="{x:Bind OffVisibility}"
                                               FontFamily="{StaticResource MonoFont}"
                                               FontSize="9"
                                               CharacterSpacing="120"
                                               Foreground="{StaticResource CoalSecondaryTextBrush}"
                                               loc:Localize.Key="panel.common.commands.off" />
                                </StackPanel>

                                <StackPanel Grid.Column="1" Spacing="2">
                                    <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind Label}"
                                               Style="{StaticResource ToolMonoBodyTextStyle}"
                                               TextWrapping="Wrap" />
                                    <!-- The usage line is shown only when it adds
                                         something — i.e. when the command takes
                                         arguments. For a bare verb the shape is just
                                         the verb column repeated with its bang, and
                                         printing it twice per row is noise. -->
                                    <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind Shape}"
                                               Visibility="{x:Bind ShapeVisibility}"
                                               Style="{StaticResource ToolMonoHintTextStyle}" />
                                </StackPanel>

                                <TextBlock Grid.Column="2"
                                           Text="{x:Bind Roles}"
                                           Style="{StaticResource ToolMonoHintTextStyle}"
                                           VerticalAlignment="Top" />
                            </Grid>
                        </DataTemplate>
                    </ItemsRepeater.ItemTemplate>
                </ItemsRepeater>
            </Grid>
        </Border>
    </StackPanel>
</UserControl>
